To create a secure login form, I will use semantic HTML5 elements. Security best practices include using the `POST` method to keep credentials out of URL logs, adding `autocomplete` attributes, and utilizing `type="password"` for masking input. For validation, I will use HTML5's built-in `required` and `pattern` attributes for basic client-side checks, and implement an AJAX request using the Fetch API to prevent page reloads and handle server responses asynchronously. I will include a feedback container to display errors without revealing sensitive backend details.

